      "source_mix": "Reuters reporting plus an official policy notice. Strongest on elite-personnel structure and formal anti-conflict rules; weaker on direct personal-finance proof or public correction episodes.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "Local priors unavailable in this experiment; the decision rests on the embedded dossier only.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Xi's score sits below the middle because the file shows a highly personalized loyalist governing structure and a strong concentration of power, but it does not give a clean, ruler-specific proof of private enrichment or a direct lie-and-correction episode. The positive side is thin: the party's rule on relatives' business activity is a real anti-conflict measure on paper. The negative side is also limited by the archive: the dossier is much stronger on political consolidation than on personal financial misconduct. That combination supports a cautious mid-low score rather than a very low one.",
      "lower_anchor_rejected": "A score of 2 or 3 would require clearer proof of personal extraction or deliberate falsehood by Xi himself. This dossier is more about system personalization than direct personal corruption.",
      "higher_anchor_rejected": "A score of 5 or above would require stronger evidence of genuine separation of interests or sustained correction. The record is too centered on loyalist control to justify that.",
