      "source_mix": "Official presidential material, local and international investigative reporting, and state-media reporting on anti-corruption steps. Good on concrete action, weaker on direct personal-finance evidence.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "Local priors unavailable in this experiment; judgment uses only the dossier evidence and explicit gaps.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Tshisekedi lands in the middle because the dossier shows real anti-corruption conduct: he ordered audits, moved against Gecamines leadership, and pushed for recovery of state assets. That is more than rhetoric. The drag comes from the adviser-orbit scandal and the taped-meeting allegations, which keep the integrity question alive around his office even without a final personal finding. The evidence supports a mixed but not especially dirty record: enough positive action to stay above the low end, but not enough direct personal-candor proof to climb higher.",
